WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.910
Are we really about to head back to the wizarding
world of Harry Potter?

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:08.540
According to an anonymous report by We Got
This Covered, it could be a possibility.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:13.260
The outlet, citing anonymous sources, claims
that the studio is developing a brand-new

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:18.600
Harry Potter movie featuring the three original
stars: Daniel Radcliffe, Emma Watson,and Rupert

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.100
Grint.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:23.460
The purported project is an adaptation of
the stage play Harry Potter and the Cursed

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:26.839
Child, written by Jack Thorne from a story
he wrote with J.K.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.480
Rowling and two-time Tony Award-winning theatre
director John Tiffany.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.900
Given the stage play's success, it's not out
of the realm of reality that Warner Bros.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.960
would want to make big bucks with a feature
film adaptation.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.420
However, we can puncture quite a few holes
in this rumor.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.140
For starters, this isn't the first time we've
heard reports that Warner Bros. wants to turn

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.520
Harry Potter and the Cursed Child into a film.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:53.960
In August 2016, just two months after the
play began its London previews, New York Daily

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:58.090
News ran an article claiming that Warner Bros.
was interested in adapting the play for the

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:01.600
silver screen in a project that would debut
as soon as 2020.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:06.240
The studio was said to have hoped that Radcliffe
would board the film to reprise his most famous

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:06.740
role.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:11.360
This report started a hot fire of speculation
that began burning up social media.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:16.610
In September 2016, Warner Bros. representatives
issued a statement debunking the rumor:

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.360
"Harry Potter and the Cursed Child is a stage
play, with no plans for there to be a film."

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.800
Additionally, there's the issue of whether
Radcliffe, Watson, and Grint would genuinely

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.440
want to come back to the franchise.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.100
In a 2018 interview with The Guardian, Grint
said:

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:35.000
"It was nice to breathe the fresh air and
now I’m really enjoying stepping further

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.960
away from that blue-screen world."

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:41.480
That doesn't exactly inspire a lot of confidence
in the idea that Grint would be willing to

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:44.200
come back to the Harry Potter universe for
another movie.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:48.440
For his part, Radcliffe has said that he's
not really interested in appearing again as

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:49.240
Harry Potter.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.600
"Oh God I've still got these on.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:51.680
I don't need these.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:52.720
They're just for the character."

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:56.440
It also seems like he's done with the character
in more ways than one.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:01.360
In November 2018, Radcliffe admitted that
he had no intention of ever watching Harry

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:05.740
Potter and the Cursed Child, since he would
feel like he was being monitored for his reaction.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:10.500
"I feel like it would not be a relaxing evening
at the theater.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.140
I feel like I would be being watched for my
reaction."

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.780
Those comments pose an important question:
If Radcliffe doesn't even want to see the

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.820
play, why would he want to be in a film adaptation
of it?

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:25.900
Unsurprisingly, Watson has taken a similar
stance as her Potter co-stars on the matter.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:30.900
Asked during a SiriusXM interview if she would
ever return to the wizarding word, Watson

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:31.500
answered,

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.560
"Ask me in another 10 years."

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:38.260
Since Warner Bros. suffered disappointment
with the less-than-fantastic performance of

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:42.630
Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald,
it's possible that the studio is looking to

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:46.630
get its Potter-verse back on track by finally
going through with Harry Potter and the Cursed

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:47.120
Child.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.840
It's also possible that the studio was willing
to spend whatever money it took to convince

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:55.599
Radcliffe, Grint, and Watson to join the film,
knowing that their involvement would boost

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:56.849
audience interest.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:01.160
Though the three stars have done well for
themselves outside the Potter franchise, none

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:04.910
have reached the same level of success they
attained during their time as witches and

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:05.480
wizards.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:10.430
With what might have been major money on the
table and the promise of even more success,

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:14.569
it's possible that Radcliffe, Grint, and Watson
really might accept an offer to star in Harry

00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:16.120
Potter and the Cursed Child.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:20.660
Still, there's nothing that's actually been
confirmed, and Cursed Child representatives

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.660
in New York reportedly declared on September
5,

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:26.440
"There are no plans whatsoever for a movie."

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:30.739
If anything comes out to make this rumor more
credible, rest assured that we'll fill you

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.180
in with all the details.

